WEBVTT

00:12.440 --> 00:15.240
I've waited so long for this moment.

00:15.240 --> 00:19.360
I sacrificed so much to see you completed.

00:19.360 --> 00:23.000
Yet you think you alone deserve to be happy?

00:23.430 --> 00:25.000
Screw you!

00:25.270 --> 00:30.600
Because of you, she continues to call out 
to the Travelers from within a deep sleep.

00:25.600 --> 00:31.010
<i>I love you... I love you...</i>

00:31.010 --> 00:32.260
"She"?

00:33.010 --> 00:36.660
I'm going to kill your friends one at a time.

00:36.660 --> 00:40.640
Taste the agony of losing 
what's important to you!

00:55.130 --> 00:56.030
What's going on?

00:56.260 --> 00:58.080
The <i>Archimedes</i> is moving.

01:01.940 --> 01:03.840
We're advancing to the final four!

01:03.840 --> 01:08.540
I can't believe how powerful my poison 
needles were when I didn't even transform!

01:09.460 --> 01:12.960
I'll ride this momentum 
and subjugate all humans!

01:12.960 --> 01:14.440
Breaking news!

01:15.300 --> 01:19.800
The match on the northern 
side has just concluded.

01:19.800 --> 01:23.030
Team Mad Dog has abandoned the match.

01:23.030 --> 01:25.310
Team FUG is victorious!

01:25.310 --> 01:27.830
We have more news to report.

01:27.830 --> 01:32.330
Four participants, 
including Jue Viole Grace,

01:32.330 --> 01:34.450
<i>have left Team FUG.</i>

01:34.450 --> 01:40.680
<i>Ron Mei and Baragav of Team 
Mad Dog have taken their place.</i>

01:40.680 --> 01:42.080
What?!

01:42.080 --> 01:44.580
<i>What's going on?</i>

01:45.200 --> 01:47.580
The Thorn of Enryu, huh?

01:47.580 --> 01:51.710
<i>FUG has found something rather interesting.</i>

01:51.710 --> 01:55.780
<i>So that was their goal 
in this Workshop Battle.</i>

01:55.780 --> 01:57.270
There you go again.

01:57.270 --> 01:58.890
You already knew, didn't you?

01:59.270 --> 02:04.450
<i>As requested, I'll leave the 
Workshop Battle in your hands.</i>

02:04.450 --> 02:06.980
<i>What will you do now?</i>

02:07.290 --> 02:11.160
As long as they don't cross 
the line, I'll simply observe.

02:14.020 --> 02:18.490
How will that boy overcome 
these adverse circumstances?

02:19.370 --> 02:21.990
Though I am curious to see

02:22.380 --> 02:25.010
the power of the real Thorn.

03:56.000 --> 04:00.010
<b>Episode 21</b>

03:56.000 --> 04:00.010
<b>The Beginning of Dawn</b>

04:03.510 --> 04:06.570
Why would Viole do that?

04:06.570 --> 04:07.630
<i>Shibisu!</i>

04:12.470 --> 04:16.260
We have to stop the creation 
of such a terrible weapon.

04:16.260 --> 04:17.780
<i>Terrible weapon?</i>

04:18.490 --> 04:19.940
What are you talking about?

04:19.940 --> 04:21.920
<i>There's no time. We have to hurry.</i>

04:21.920 --> 04:24.040
<i>Viole is—no.</i>

04:24.240 --> 04:25.550
Bam is in danger.

04:25.900 --> 04:27.030
What?!

04:27.760 --> 04:30.890
The black turtle left the team?!

04:30.890 --> 04:32.360
Don't be absurd!

04:32.360 --> 04:34.920
The black turtle wouldn't do that!

04:34.920 --> 04:39.310
Yeah! He wouldn't abandon 
Horyang and the others,

04:39.310 --> 04:41.620
even if he's FUG and a bad person.

04:41.620 --> 04:43.700
He's not a bad turtle, Bun Turtle!

04:43.700 --> 04:45.680
H-He totally is!

04:45.960 --> 04:47.610
In any case, let's get confirmation.

04:48.250 --> 04:50.150
Gator, hide your face.

04:51.720 --> 04:54.810
Well, this place looks nicer than I expected.

04:56.110 --> 04:57.870
I'm gonna burn it all.

04:57.870 --> 04:59.060
Don't, idiot!

04:59.380 --> 05:00.340
<i>Bam...</i>

05:06.420 --> 05:10.330
I have been waiting for you, 
final four team members.

05:10.700 --> 05:13.830
I am R-9, your robot assistant.

05:14.490 --> 05:16.360
I have prepared a room for you.

05:16.360 --> 05:19.840
Please make yourselves at 
home until the match begins.

05:20.120 --> 05:22.270
Can I burn this, too?

05:22.270 --> 05:23.710
Don't, idiot.

05:26.220 --> 05:29.220
I'm gonna look for something to burn!

05:29.770 --> 05:30.740
Hey.

05:30.740 --> 05:35.730
Where should I go to watch the recording 
of the Team FUG versus Team Mad Dog match?

05:36.110 --> 05:39.470
The match recording can be 
viewed in the video room.

05:40.230 --> 05:43.130
Okay. I'm going to review the recording.

05:43.130 --> 05:45.110
You guys head to the room.

05:47.220 --> 05:49.150
What the hell happened?

05:49.720 --> 05:52.120
Why would Viole leave the team?

05:52.970 --> 05:55.300
The black turtle wouldn't run.

05:55.300 --> 05:58.620
This must be FUG's doing.

05:58.900 --> 06:00.230
You're right.

06:00.570 --> 06:04.310
But FUG made a bet with us, so why?

06:04.710 --> 06:07.110
They can't be trusted.

06:07.510 --> 06:10.720
We don't know what they're planning.

06:11.700 --> 06:12.970
Obviously.

06:12.970 --> 06:16.460
I wish I could crack their 
heads open right now.

06:17.390 --> 06:20.060
This tournament is nothing special.

06:21.480 --> 06:25.820
The snake woman said she'd pay 
us if we made it to the final.

06:25.820 --> 06:27.990
I guess we'll cooperate until then.

06:28.370 --> 06:31.240
Anyway, I heard Viole fled.

06:33.390 --> 06:35.990
He was just a coward after all.

06:36.230 --> 06:39.250
Maybe he got scared of the Mad Dog and ran.

06:39.250 --> 06:43.090
Does that mean the Mad Dog 
is the new Slayer Candidate?

06:44.750 --> 06:46.860
Who are those guys?

06:46.860 --> 06:49.670
You don't know the first thing about Viole.

06:49.670 --> 06:52.990
I'll kill them if we face 
them in the semifinals.

06:56.180 --> 06:57.930
Wh-What's wrong?

06:57.930 --> 07:04.060
Th-Th-There's a h-huge bug in the room!

07:08.780 --> 07:11.090
That's one massive moth!

07:14.160 --> 07:20.070
<i>The semifinal between Team Mad Dog 
and Team FUG has finally begun!</i>

07:20.070 --> 07:21.030
<i>Against expectations,</i>

07:21.030 --> 07:25.290
<i>the match is progressing without any 
major contact between the teams.</i>

07:25.290 --> 07:30.300
<i>Where is Viole going on his own?</i>

07:30.300 --> 07:34.150
<i>As soon as the match began, Bam left FUG.</i>

07:34.150 --> 07:36.830
<i>At the same time, Novick disappeared.</i>

07:36.830 --> 07:40.020
<i>Why did the Mad Dog choose to work with FUG?</i>

07:40.730 --> 07:43.820
<i>And where did Bam go?</i>

07:43.820 --> 07:46.860
Are you looking for your missing friend,

07:47.810 --> 07:50.070
Khun Aguero Agnes?

07:50.380 --> 07:53.350
Mia. You made it to the final four?

07:53.900 --> 07:55.760
But how do you know my name?

07:55.760 --> 07:57.330
I've known from the start.

07:57.330 --> 07:58.330
What?

07:59.500 --> 08:04.640
FUG entered three Gamblers 
in this Workshop Battle.

08:04.980 --> 08:07.340
I'm one of them.

08:07.910 --> 08:12.830
We're hunters FUG sent to catch you guys.

08:13.320 --> 08:16.800
There's no need to hide your 
face with that mask anymore...

08:18.350 --> 08:22.500
because you'll soon fall 
into an eternal sleep.

08:30.910 --> 08:32.950
<i>Was it all a trap?</i>

08:33.360 --> 08:36.540
<i>Then what about our bet with FUG?</i>

08:37.870 --> 08:40.210
<i>Why did they bring Bam here?</i>

08:40.210 --> 08:42.110
<i>Damn it. What should I do?</i>

08:42.720 --> 08:43.600
Khun!

08:48.010 --> 08:49.630
You idiot.

08:49.870 --> 08:51.150
Shibisu...

08:57.970 --> 09:05.770
Kill... Kill... Kill...

09:13.230 --> 09:16.030
So you trapped Viole inside there?

09:17.580 --> 09:23.270
You're the one who offered me freedom 
in exchange for working with FUG.

09:23.800 --> 09:27.920
And don't you despise Viole,

09:28.380 --> 09:30.670
Beniamino Cassano?

09:32.680 --> 09:34.090
Whatever.

09:34.090 --> 09:39.420
I don't care about you or FUG's goals 
as long as you keep your promises.

09:39.420 --> 09:44.930
I just want him to suffer like I did.

09:46.150 --> 09:51.500
I'm going to kill every last 
one of his precious friends.

10:06.470 --> 10:07.500
Where am I?

10:10.450 --> 10:12.570
Did I fall to the bottom?

10:18.700 --> 10:20.520
<i>I can't use my Shinsu.</i>

10:20.520 --> 10:24.260
For your own sake, you shouldn't 
think about it too much,

10:25.860 --> 10:28.230
Jue Viole Grace.

10:28.660 --> 10:29.820
You...

10:30.500 --> 10:31.370
Is this...

10:31.730 --> 10:36.760
We brought you here for one reason.

10:37.460 --> 10:41.990
To turn you into a weapon 
and offer you to our master.

10:43.490 --> 10:49.730
You planned to break the rules, meet 
your old teammates, and leave the team.

10:50.170 --> 10:54.500
Rather than making a boy who could 
betray us at any time into a Slayer,

10:54.750 --> 11:00.010
don't you think it's smarter to turn him 
into a weapon that won't fight back?

11:00.870 --> 11:06.520
Once the solution transported here 
by the <i>Archimedes</i> is poured here,

11:06.830 --> 11:12.520
everything except the Thorn will melt, 
and the ultimate weapon will be born.

11:12.520 --> 11:18.520
That weapon will pass into the 
hands of a master worthy of it.

11:18.970 --> 11:22.990
Please make yourself at home until then.

11:26.400 --> 11:28.790
<i>At this rate, everyone will be in danger.</i>

11:29.200 --> 11:32.670
<i>I need to find a way out of here.</i>

11:37.590 --> 11:39.170
You absolute idiot.

11:39.390 --> 11:41.430
You should've told me he was alive.

11:41.430 --> 11:43.340
Sh-Shibisu, wait!

11:45.280 --> 11:48.010
I wouldn't run if I were you.

11:48.010 --> 11:49.020
Hatz...

11:49.330 --> 11:51.480
We know everything.

11:51.790 --> 11:54.170
Did you get a new weapon since 
the last time I saw you?

11:54.510 --> 11:56.730
Do you know how to pull the trigger?

11:58.480 --> 12:00.200
I see you haven't changed.

12:01.000 --> 12:02.650
I came because I have urgent business.

12:04.330 --> 12:05.910
Bam's life is in danger.

12:06.200 --> 12:08.410
Wh-What do you mean?

12:08.410 --> 12:11.410
How do you know Bam is alive?

12:11.770 --> 12:13.420
Lero Ro told me.

12:13.780 --> 12:14.560
What?

12:15.290 --> 12:18.420
Lero Ro snuck onto the <i>Archimedes</i>.

12:20.140 --> 12:24.180
That's where he learned about 
FUG and the Workshop's plan.

12:24.740 --> 12:26.180
What do they want?

12:26.180 --> 12:29.930
To melt living humans and 
create an Ignition Weapon.

12:29.930 --> 12:30.690
Wha—

12:31.090 --> 12:33.270
FUG intends to melt one further

12:33.270 --> 12:36.990
to create an Ignition Weapon that 
possesses the power of an Irregular.

12:37.310 --> 12:38.770
You mean...

12:38.770 --> 12:40.450
They're going to melt Bam.

12:40.800 --> 12:42.530
We need to save him.

12:42.530 --> 12:44.670
How dare you?!

12:44.670 --> 12:48.530
I'm a honeybee who's here 
to rule the human world!

12:48.750 --> 12:49.660
Get out!

12:49.660 --> 12:53.510
I'll smash you, Moth Monster!

12:53.510 --> 12:54.280
Gator!

12:55.950 --> 12:57.610
B-Blue Turtle?

12:57.610 --> 12:59.920
All of you, come with me.

13:03.640 --> 13:07.760
What? They're going to turn the 
black turtle into a weapon?

13:08.770 --> 13:10.840
Wh-What does that even mean?

13:10.840 --> 13:12.270
Turn Viole into a weapon?

13:12.530 --> 13:13.900
Is that true?

13:14.790 --> 13:19.270
Warrior Turtle, you show up out of the 
blue, and that's what you have to say?

13:19.870 --> 13:22.250
It's all true, Rak.

13:22.560 --> 13:25.900
Bam is being held in the mountains.

13:25.900 --> 13:27.660
You're kidding.

13:28.450 --> 13:32.490
Why did you wait until now to 
tell us if you knew, you idiot?

13:32.490 --> 13:37.800
If we'd known sooner, we could've stopped 
them before the black turtle was captured!

13:37.800 --> 13:40.130
Say something, Warrior Turtle!

13:40.660 --> 13:41.750
Well...

13:44.010 --> 13:47.080
I'm sorry. I couldn't stop them.

13:51.760 --> 13:54.770
Khun, you know what this means, don't you?

13:55.040 --> 13:59.490
You know why Hatz and Ro couldn't tell 
us as soon as they learned the truth.

14:00.950 --> 14:05.170
There are FUG Rankers on 
the <i>Archimedes</i> right now.

14:06.060 --> 14:10.530
They're probably watching all our 
communications and movements.

14:10.530 --> 14:13.030
Even if we'd known sooner,

14:13.340 --> 14:16.540
there wasn't anything we 
could've done on that ship.

14:16.880 --> 14:21.290
In fact, we might've acted carelessly 
and put everyone in danger.

14:22.300 --> 14:27.060
I know why FUG didn't try harder 
to stop us from coming here.

14:28.080 --> 14:33.190
We were hostages to keep Bam in line.

14:33.920 --> 14:36.510
Damn it. They'll pay for this.

14:37.100 --> 14:40.810
How dare they ruin our reunion like this?

14:50.750 --> 14:54.440
They haven't ruined it yet, Shibisu.

14:56.240 --> 15:01.080
The party can wait until 
after the game is over.

15:01.660 --> 15:04.580
Nobody knows who will be smiling then.

15:05.110 --> 15:11.470
Ro realized this game was our only chance.

15:11.470 --> 15:13.770
If the game doesn't start...

15:14.940 --> 15:17.600
then what could be won can't be won.

15:17.600 --> 15:20.100
Damn it! I can't take it anymore!

15:20.320 --> 15:22.940
I'm going to rescue the 
black turtle right now!

15:22.940 --> 15:24.610
You can't! Wait!

15:24.610 --> 15:25.940
Rak, wait!

15:28.230 --> 15:31.990
Hey, gator. Where do you think 
you're going by yourself?

15:31.990 --> 15:34.160
To the black turtle!

15:34.160 --> 15:37.940
Don't think you can stop me, Blue Turtle!

15:37.940 --> 15:39.160
I'll go with you.

15:39.160 --> 15:41.550
All right! Wait, what?

15:42.240 --> 15:46.500
Hatz, how long until the <i>Archimedes</i> 
arrives at Bam's location?

15:47.590 --> 15:49.440
Probably about two hours.

15:49.820 --> 15:53.510
Lero Ro said he'd do what 
he could to delay it.

15:53.510 --> 15:57.100
Okay. We're going to rescue Bam.

15:57.100 --> 16:01.020
That said, we won't give 
up the tournament, either.

16:03.710 --> 16:07.060
We're going to summon Bam.

16:09.390 --> 16:12.490
<i>Emergency! We have an emergency situation!</i>

16:13.430 --> 16:16.810
<i>A system malfunction has 
allowed detainees to escape!</i>

16:17.130 --> 16:19.460
<i>It will take time to restore the system.</i>

16:23.720 --> 16:26.590
<i>You've managed to buy some time, Ro.</i>

16:27.080 --> 16:29.540
<i>Are they really okay?</i>

16:29.950 --> 16:33.900
They'll be fine. I sent Hatz to them.

16:34.560 --> 16:39.310
I'm confident he'll tell 
his friends the truth.

16:39.310 --> 16:42.450
The rest is up to them.

16:43.220 --> 16:46.460
We'll do what we can.

16:46.460 --> 16:47.600
<i>Roger that.</i>

16:48.820 --> 16:51.370
<i>We mustn't give up.</i>

16:51.680 --> 16:56.070
<i>Once the game begins,
there will be a way to win.</i>

16:57.420 --> 17:00.790
It's rather noisy outside.

17:01.160 --> 17:04.140
There's a problem at the detention facility.

17:04.140 --> 17:07.070
Some of the detainees have escaped.

17:07.540 --> 17:10.800
It will delay our work somewhat.

17:12.420 --> 17:14.420
Shall we dispose of them?

17:14.840 --> 17:16.290
No, it's fine.

17:16.690 --> 17:19.800
What's important is the tournament's outcome.

17:19.800 --> 17:23.390
Stay put until the match ends.

17:23.390 --> 17:24.170
Yes, sir.

17:24.990 --> 17:28.620
<i>They waited until the 
match began to do this.</i>

17:29.140 --> 17:36.950
<i>Do they believe the boys in the 
arena will be able to do something?</i>

17:39.760 --> 17:41.000
<i>Emily...</i>

17:44.770 --> 17:47.680
Thank you for waiting, everyone.

17:47.680 --> 17:51.840
The tournament semifinals will now begin.

17:53.340 --> 17:58.020
Participants, please get ready on the field.

17:58.990 --> 18:01.070
Summon Bam?

18:01.740 --> 18:05.600
Khun, will this strategy really work?

18:05.600 --> 18:08.520
This plan has too many uncertainties.

18:08.880 --> 18:10.360
<i>I know.</i>

18:10.360 --> 18:12.190
But we have to try.

18:12.530 --> 18:19.200
It's probably the only way for us to 
rescue Bam while following the rules.

18:21.160 --> 18:23.770
What?! Summon Viole?

18:23.770 --> 18:28.570
Yeah. There's no way they'll let us 
break the rules to bring Bam back.

18:29.520 --> 18:33.090
They can't afford to give FUG 
an opportunity to interfere.

18:33.750 --> 18:39.190
Considering the future, we have to 
follow the rules, no matter what.

18:39.520 --> 18:41.260
Isn't that right, Hatz?

18:41.530 --> 18:44.360
That's what Lero Ro said to tell you.

18:44.360 --> 18:47.220
He said he'd take care of 
the rest if we did that.

18:47.830 --> 18:50.320
But how are we supposed to summon Viole?

18:50.920 --> 18:52.770
Hasn't he been captured?

18:53.080 --> 18:58.280
Besides Viole, three others 
have left Team FUG.

18:58.650 --> 19:03.530
Horyang, Novick, and Team FUG's Scout.

19:03.990 --> 19:09.040
They betrayed FUG and are 
planning to help Viole escape.

19:10.020 --> 19:12.250
What?! How do you know that?

19:12.250 --> 19:16.250
Emily told me. Look.

19:17.440 --> 19:20.360
<b>Handsome</b>

19:17.730 --> 19:21.110
<b>Where is Novick?</b>

19:18.570 --> 19:20.250
I-Is this...

19:19.510 --> 19:23.010
<b>Emily</b>

19:19.650 --> 19:23.010
<b>Attempting to rescue Viole with Horyang.</b>

19:20.070 --> 19:23.010
<b>Emily</b>

19:20.250 --> 19:23.010
It's a program that answers questions.

19:20.360 --> 19:23.010
<b>Please prepare to summon.</b>

19:23.600 --> 19:28.020
I thought it might work, and this is 
the answer it gave me when I asked.

19:28.650 --> 19:32.200
If this information was uploaded into Emily,

19:32.200 --> 19:37.330
then one of the three who left the 
team must've sent us a message.

19:37.330 --> 19:41.030
They're definitely on Bam's side.

19:41.680 --> 19:44.420
H-Horyang, too?

19:46.720 --> 19:49.620
The chances are slim, but it's possible.

19:49.620 --> 19:53.100
If they successfully free Bam,

19:53.720 --> 19:56.600
then we can summon him here.

19:57.540 --> 20:01.130
Can we trust whoever sent that message?

20:01.850 --> 20:04.940
Aren't some of them working for FUG?

20:04.940 --> 20:07.560
<i>This is our only option right now.</i>

20:07.990 --> 20:12.170
I don't know what they want,
but I'm certain they're on Bam's side.

20:12.740 --> 20:16.120
Novick is with them, too. 
We have to trust them.

20:16.690 --> 20:21.660
I've never heard someone express so much 
doubt over trusting someone before.

20:21.660 --> 20:22.920
I agree.

20:22.920 --> 20:27.580
After all, I thought he'd really died.

20:30.730 --> 20:32.950
Can you really communicate 
with them that way?

20:32.950 --> 20:34.080
Yes.

20:34.710 --> 20:38.090
As long as we share a keyword.

20:38.480 --> 20:40.360
How strange.

20:40.360 --> 20:42.090
Will they figure it out?

20:42.310 --> 20:43.580
Yes, probably.

20:44.470 --> 20:46.780
He's an exceptional Regular, after all.

20:49.310 --> 20:53.100
We have until they make 
it possible to summon Bam

20:53.680 --> 20:57.640
to finish preparing to summon him.

20:57.640 --> 21:00.030
It'll be a contest of speed.

21:02.630 --> 21:04.500
A fight! A fight!

21:04.500 --> 21:06.290
Why do I have to go with him?

21:06.290 --> 21:11.370
As our first member, Wangnan will 
sprint to the destination with Quaetro.

21:11.760 --> 21:15.120
Once you're ready,
begin summoning right away.

21:15.630 --> 21:19.150
The gator and Yihwa will deal with 
any enemies while supporting you.

21:20.010 --> 21:22.630
Gather points as quickly as possible.

21:23.060 --> 21:26.130
Akraptor will stay hidden while he moves.

21:26.670 --> 21:30.140
Take out their first member 
at the critical moment.

21:30.840 --> 21:32.730
Team Shibisu will stand by.

21:33.250 --> 21:35.990
We don't know who our opponents are yet,

21:35.990 --> 21:37.930
but we need you to handle 
them if it comes to it.

21:37.930 --> 21:39.150
Got it.

21:39.380 --> 21:41.370
We haven't used this kind 
of teamwork in a while.

21:41.830 --> 21:43.650
Reminds me of the past.

21:43.900 --> 21:47.530
It's not time to reminisce yet, Shibisu.

21:48.910 --> 21:52.040
The match will begin shortly.

21:52.040 --> 21:56.040
Regulars, please get ready.

